From: djvalic <djvalic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:58:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] touch: the hold to calibrate holds up on the resistive panel

Follow-up to the previous two patches (PR #91), after a second review:

- The resistive TSC2007 panel: under load its readings slow to 70 ms and
  more, and one released reading among them ended the press (the gap was
  70 ms). A lift of up to 200 ms (kCalibrationHoldGapMs, from the last
  pressed reading to the next) is now bridged, but the lifts of 70 ms and
  more (kCalibrationHoldNoiseMs) are counted: more than 3
  (kCalibrationHoldMaxLifts) in one hold are taps, and the hold starts
  again at the press after the last one, so 10 s of taps still never fire.
  A release seen and then a press after the gap still starts a new press.
- One far-off sample no longer starts the 10 s again: 2 pressed readings
  in a row outside the radius (kCalibrationHoldMovedReadings) do, timed
  from the first of them.
- The gesture's numbers are all in touch_hold_gesture.h (the wrapper
  header includes it); TouchHoldGesture takes the screen size for the
  radius. Holds started again for taps or for moving are logged at debug
  level.
- The first-run tour sits on the top layer with a dim layer that takes
  every touch: a hold during it opened calibration underneath, out of
  reach. The tour is now ended first (FirstRunTour::abandon(), not marked
  completed, so it is offered again).
- Refused while the PIN lock screen or the PIN pad is up (no way past a
  PIN), and while the busy overlay or the abort dialog covers the screen.
- The wizard step is reached through the guard Next and Back use
  (ui_wizard_request_step): a Next or ui_wizard_advance() that comes while
  it is pending is dropped, and the hold is refused while a step change is
  pending (ui_wizard_is_navigating).
- Both paths decide with touch_hold_action() at the hold and again on the
  next tick, in the same order; the tour is ended and dialogs are closed
  only when something opens. So the overlay path, too, re-checks that no
  wizard is active.
- force_touch_calibration_step(true) is reset when the touch step is left
  and when the wizard ends, so later navigation counts the steps as usual
  and the "Force-showing" log stops.
- A targeted wizard session (Settings > Printer > Run Setup Wizard) has no
  touch step: when it has a cancel callback (all of them do), it is ended
  with it, as Back on its first step (ui_wizard_cancel_session), and the
  overlay opens a tick later; without one the hold still does nothing.

Known, not changed here: a dialog that opens after the sweep, before the
calibration is up, can still cover it; and, in upstream HelixScreen, a
bad preview on the wizard's own touch step has no quick way back (the hold
is off there on purpose), so only a restart gets out of it.

Tests in test_kiln_touch_hold.cpp: 1, 2 and 3 bridged lifts of up to
200 ms fire and 4 do not; lifts under 70 ms are not counted; one far-off
sample does not move the hold and two in a row do; slow readings (70, 85,
100 ms) with one released reading keep it; taps at 10 to 100 ms readings,
regular and irregular, never fire; the stale start; the lock screen, busy,
pending navigation, targeted-session and tour decisions; and an abandoned
tour is not completed and is offered again.

Upstream: not applicable (Kiln OS specific)
